ה אוכל את הצב הנמוך.","en":"The tall bear is eating the short turtle.","alt":[],"t":"l"},{"he":"הכלבים הנמוכים אוכלים חתולים.","en":"The short dogs eat cats.","alt":[],"t":"l"},{"he":"הילד הגדול רואֶה את הילדה הקטנה.","en":"The big boy sees the little girl.","alt":[],"t":"l"},{"he":"הילדות שלו לא מהירוֹת, הן איטיות.","en":"His girls aren't fast, they're slow.","alt":[],"t":"t"}],"hints":{"קר":"cold (sg. masc.) / cold","חדש":"new","יבש":"dry","מלא":"filled / full (sg. masc.) / total","קטן":"little (sg. masc.) / small (sg. masc.) / small","ריק":"empty","איטי":"slow","ארוך":"long","קרוב":"close / near","רחוק":"far (sg. masc.) / far away / far","רטוב":"wet","דג":"a fish / fish","זה":"it / it is / it's","דרך":"path / road / way","ריקה":"empty (sg. fem.)","חתול":"a cat / cat","אהבה":"love","חדשה":"new (sg. fem.)","היא":"her / it / she","גבוהה":"high (sg. fem.) / tall (sg. fem.) / taller","גבוה":"tall, high","אני":"I / I am / I am a girl","לא":"aren't / didn't / do not","גדול":"big","הכלב":"the dog","ספר":"a book / book / tell! (Story)","קצר":"short, brief (Length, time)","אנחנו":"we / we are / we (c.p)","אישה":"a woman / wife / woman","שלו":"his / its","הספרים":"the books / the books are","זאת":"it is (feminine) / that / that is (feminine)","דקה":"minute","ארוכה":"long (sg. fem.)","גדולה":"big / great / large","שלי":"mine / my","אוהב":"like / likes / love","מיץ":"a glass of juice / juice","הילד":"the boy / the boy is / the kid","הם":"are / they / they are","ילדים":"boys / children / kids","שלךָ":"your (sg.masc.) / yours (sg.masc.) / your (m.s)","יש":"I have / do you have / has","לי":"I have / for me / me","עוגה":"a cake / cake","הוא":"(he) is / (it) is / he","שותֶה":"drink / drinking / drinks","יין":"wine","חם":"hot, warm (m.s) / hot","שלהם":"their / theirs / their (m)","קורא":"is reading / read / reading","אוכלת":"are eating / eating / is eating","לחם":"bread","רוצָה":"want / wants / would like","אתה":"you / you are / you (m.s)","הנמוך":"the short (sg. masc.)","אוכל":"eat / eating / eats","כריך":"a sandwich / sandwich","גדר":"fence","המשאית":"the truck","של":"'s / Abraham's / avraham's","אברהם":"Abraham / Abraham's / avraham","מים":"water","רוצֶה":"want / wants / would like","פירות":"fruit","את":"it / that / the fruit","הקפה":"the coffee / the coffee is","אתם":"do you want / you / you are","האישה":"the woman / the woman is","רואָה":"is seeing / see / sees","הגבר":"the man / the man is","רוסיה":"Russia","אוכלים":"are eating / eat / eating","חתולים":"cat / cats","הגדול":"biggest / the big (sg. masc.) / the greatest","רואֶה":"is seeing / see / sees","הילדה":"the girl / the girl is","מהירוֹת":"fast / speed / the speed of light","הן":"are / they / they are"},"words":[{"he":"של","en":"Abraham's","alt":["'s","Avraham's","of","whose"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"shel"},{"he":"גבוהה","en":"taller","alt":["high (sg. fem.)","tall (sg. fem.)"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"ריקה","en":"empty (sg. fem.)","alt":[],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"רחוק","en":"far away","alt":["far (sg. masc.)"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"rakhok"},{"he":"דרך","en":"path","alt":["road","way"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"derekh"},{"he":"ארוכה","en":"long (sg. fem.)","alt":[],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"המשאית","en":"the truck","alt":[],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"אברהם","en":"Abraham","alt":["Abraham's","Avraham","Avraham's"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"מהירוֹת","en":"Speed, Velocity","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"m'hirut"},{"he":"יבש","en":"Dry","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"yavesh"},{"he":"קצר","en":"Short, Brief (Length, Time)","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"katzar"},{"he":"רטוב","en":"Wet","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"ratuv"},{"he":"ריק","en":"Empty","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"reik"},{"he":"קר","en":"cold (sg. masc.)","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"kar"},{"he":"מלא","en":"total","alt":["filled","full (sg. masc.)"],"from":"skill","tr":"male"},{"he":"גבוה","en":"Tall, High","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"gavoah"},{"he":"זה","en":"that","alt":["it's","this"],"from":"phrase","tr":"zeh"},{"he":"זאת","en":"this","alt":["this is (feminine)","that is (feminine)"],"from":"phrase","tr":"zot"},{"he":"היא","en":"she","alt":["her","it"],"from":"phrase","tr":"hi"}],"lexemes":["קרובים","קרובה","מהירוֹת","גבוהה","יבש","מהירים","והתפוח","קצר","הכריך","רטוב","קצרה","רטובים","קרים","ריק","יבשים","גבוהים","רטובה","קר","המשאית","מלאים","מלא","הגבוה","גבוה","ריקה","קרה","יבשה","והילדה","מהירה"],"tips":"**Copula (אוגד)**\n------------\nWhen we want to define a **general** feature of an object (i.e. lemons are sour), we use the **copula** (אוגד).\nThe main purpose of the copula is to link the *subject* of a sentence with a *predicate*.\n\nIn simple terms, the copula is like the English verb \"to be\".\n\nThe copula in Hebrew uses the third person pronouns to describe objects (i.e.  \nhe/it הוא  \nshe/it היא  \nthey (m) הם  \nthey (f) הן).\n\nFor example:\n\nFish **are** tasty = דגים **הם** טעימים (literally -  fish **they (are)** tasty).\n\nThis allows you to differentiate between:  \nדגים טעימים - tasty fish  \nand  \nדגים הם טעימים - fish are tasty.\n\n**Definite articles with adjectives**\n------------\nWhen adding definite articles to nouns with adjectives, **both** the noun and the adjective receive a definite article.\n\nFor example:\n\nThe big dog = **ה**כלב **ה**גדול (**ha**kélev **ha**gadól).\n\nThis rule is also applicable when we use more than one adjective for the same noun.\n\nThe big beautiful dog = **ה**כלב **ה**גדול **וה**יפה (**ha**kélev **ha**gadól **ve'ha**yafé).  \nNote that we say \"big *and* beautiful\". הגדול היפה is not as natural as \"big beautiful\" as in English.\n\nSo now you can differentiate between: \n\n* הכלב גדול = The dog is big (ha'kelev gadol)\n\n* הכלב **ה**גדול = The big dog (ha'kelev **ha**'gadol)\n\n**Possessives with adjectives**\n-----------------\nWhen you have a noun, an (attributive) adjective and a possessive, the possessive comes after both the noun and the adjective:\n\nהכלב החדש שלי  \nMy new dog\n\n*not* הכלב שלי החדש"}